title: NetBird: API Token (Personal Access Token)
agents: netbird
catalog: cloud/netbird
license: GPLv3
distribution: check_mk

item:
 {User}/{Token name} for service users, {[user] User}/{Token name} for regular users
 (only if enabled in the special agent rule).

description:
 This check monitors one NetBird personal access token. Two conditions are
 evaluated and the worse state wins:

 {Remaining lifetime}: {WARN} at 30 days, {CRIT} at 7 days by default. A token that
 is already expired is {CRIT}. Optionally an expired token is ignored (service
 {OK}) once it has been expired for longer than a configurable time.

 {Unused since}: {WARN} if the token was not used for 90 days (default), no {CRIT}
 by default. A token that was never used counts from its creation date and the text
 says "never used".

 All thresholds can be configured with the rule "NetBird token".

 Metrics: days until expiry, days since last use.

discovery:
 One service is created per token. Tokens can be included or excluded by a regular
 expression on the token name with the rule "NetBird token discovery", for example
 to leave out spare tokens.
